"text": "This was Tesla's Roadster reveal on October 15th, at SpaceX's test site in McGregor, Texas. Everything you're seeing is a controlled stunt on a closed course, not a car on a public street. The car drove up a curved ramp and stopped, upside down, for a few seconds. On another run, it launched off, rolled itself upright, and set down on the pavement. It even hopped over five Tesla vehicles, a Semi included. And in the driver's seat? An Optimus robot, which Engadget reports was only there for show. The stunts were programmed into the car. This Roadster was first promised back in 2017. Tesla now says production starts in 2028.",
